(19, 'hair transplant in nepal - Dr.Rajan Tajhya | Aakar Dermatology', 'hair-transplant-in-nepal', 'hair', 'hair', 'services/hair-transplant-in-nepal-63e7bdb0cae7907d.png', 'window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);} gtag(\'consent\', \'default\', {\"ad_personalization\":\"denied\",\"ad_storage\":\"denied\",\"ad_user_data\"', '<div><!-- primary start -->\r\n\r\n						\n<article>\n\n	<div>\n\n		\n		<header>\n			<h3>hair transplant in nepal</h3>		</header><!-- .entry-header -->\n\n		<p><a href=\"https://drrajanskinclinic.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/hair-transplant-in-nepal.png\"><img width=\"300\" height=\"107\" src=\"http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hair-transplant-in-nepal-63e7bdb0cae7907d.png\" alt=\"hair transplant in nepal\" srcset=\"http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hair-transplant-in-nepal-63e7bdb0cae7907d.png 300w, http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hair-transplant-in-nepal-7c49ee9262589699.png 1024w, http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hair-transplant-in-nepal-d559b15803515605.png 768w, http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hair-transplant-in-nepal-4415b2ceaa275815.png 1120w\"></a></p>\n\n	</div><!-- .entry-content -->\n\n	</article><!-- #post-3263 -->\n\n<div>\n\n		<div>\n		<h3>Leave a Reply <small><a href=\"/our-services/hair-transplant-in-nepal/hair-transplant-in-nepal/#respond\">Cancel reply</a></small></h3>	</div><!-- #respond -->\n	\n</div><!-- #comments -->\n\r\n					</div>', 'hair transplant in nepal - Dr.Rajan Tajhya | Aakar Dermatology | Dr. Rajan Tajhya Skin Clinic', 'window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);} gtag(\'consent\', \'default\', {\"ad_personalization\":\"denied\",\"ad_storage\":\"denied\",\"ad_user_data\"', 0, 1, 40, '2026-10-03 11:07:56', '2026-10-03 11:13:35'),
(20, 'Hydra Facial in Nepal', 'hydra-facial-in-nepal', 'skin', 'skin', 'services/hydra-facial-in-nepal-532de482d1d2228b.png', '&quot;Revitalize your skin with HydraFacial treatment at Dr Rajan Clinic in Lalitpur. Enjoy glowing, hydrated skin, suitable for all skin types!', '<div><!-- primary start -->\r\n\r\n						\n<article>\n\n	<div>\n\n		<img width=\"640\" height=\"229\" src=\"http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hydra-facial-in-nepal-532de482d1d2228b.png\" alt=\"Hydra Facial\" title=\"Hydra Facial\" srcset=\"http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hydra-facial-in-nepal-532de482d1d2228b.png 1024w, http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hydra-facial-in-nepal-73d29064780580ad.png 300w, http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hydra-facial-in-nepal-d0cd1f179bdad792.png 768w, http://localhost:8000/storage/services/hydra-facial-in-nepal-6bee2a0303db1c68.png 1120w\">\n		<header>\n			<h3>Hydra Facial</h3>		</header><!-- .entry-header -->\n\n				<div>\n						<section>\n						<div>\n					<div>\n			<div>\n						<div>\n				<div>\n									<div>\n					<div>\n				<div>\n										<div><div></div><div><div></div></div></div>				</div>\n							</div>\n				</div>\n								</div>\n				</div>\n					</div>\n		</div>\n					</div>\n		</section>\n				<section>\n						<div>\n					<div>\n			<div>\n						<div>\n				<div>\n									<p>HydraFacial treatment is an innovative advance in non-laser skin resurfacing. It combines cleansing, exfoliation, extraction, hydration, and anti-oxidant protection at the same time to give you clearer, glowing skin.</p>\n<p>In simpler words, HydraFacial is a serum-based treatment performed under medical guidance, with a customized solution for all skin types. Also, it minimizes fine lines and wrinkles, congested or enlarged pores, hyperpigmentation, and even dark spots.</p>\n<p>HydraFacial treatment is non-invasive, painless, and non-irritating. </p>\n<p>This revolutionary treatment is made for all skin types. In the simplest of words, this is only hydrating fluid water mixed with various hydrating products. It has a minimal possibility to create allergies to the skin.</p>\n<p>While this <a href=\"https://drrajanskinclinic.com/our-services/skin-problems/\">skin treatment</a> is suitable to people of all varieties of skin, HydraFacial is especially beneficial to those with oily skin for whom other procedures are a burden.</p>\n<p>You can do this treatment at any age, with any skin type and skin issue with no side effects because it’s all about cleaning and infusing. </p>\n<h2>At our clinic, we do Hydrafacial treatment in the following essential steps:</h2>\n<h3>Cleansing and Exfoliation </h3>\n<p>The reason your skin doesn’t look healthy is that some of the cells are dead, though you won’t notice this microscopic change. So, in the very beginning, this step removes the dead cells and uncovers the smooth healthy skin underneath them. This is done using nothing but a simple ultrasonic scrubber and warm steam.</p>\n<h3>Extractions </h3>\n<p>This is a quick and completely painless extraction of blackheads &amp; whiteheads. The gentle suction force from a special vacuum tip with water makes the step effortless.</p>\n<h3>Hydration and infusion</h3>\n<p>This is a vortex fusion technology for deep penetration of antioxidants and hyaluronic acid, which eventually hydrates the skin and makes it healthy. Special HydraFacial liquids are infused based on the skin type you have. Consequently, this process hydrates and cleanses your skin.</p>\n<h3>Bipolar Radiofrequency (skin tightening) </h3>\n<p>Radio-frequency skin tightening is an aesthetic technique that uses radiofrequency (RF) energy (harmless) to heat the skin.</p>\n<p>This is done to stimulate the production of cutaneous collagen, elastin, and hyaluronic acid. Their production reduces the appearance of fine lines and loose skin. The technique promotes tissue remodeling and the production of new collagen and elastin. Both are enormously beneficial for skin health.</p>\n<h3>Customized Gelly-Rubber Face mask</h3>\n<p>The next process involves covering your face with a masking layer. We have different varieties of face masks customized to your skin needs and skin conditions.</p>\n<p>These are a few examples: Rose mask, Pearl whitening mask, Seaweed, Anti-wrinkle, Green tea, Gold mask, Hyaluronic soft, Anti spot, Collagen mask, and many more.</p>\n<h3>LED Light Therapy </h3>\n<p>Light therapy provides additional benefits after the HydraFacial treatment. This photodynamic light therapy uses a specific type of light that radiates energy and stimulates your cells. As a result, your skin’s production of collagen and elastin increases.</p>\n<h2>Is the treatment suitable for my skin type?</h2>\n<p>This revolutionary treatment is made for all skin types. In the simplest of words, this is only hydrating fluid water mixed with various hydrating products. It has a minimal possibility to create allergies to the skin.</p>\n<p>While this skin treatment is suitable to people of all varieties of skin, HydraFacial is especially beneficial to those with oily skin for whom other procedures are a burden.</p>\n<h2>How much time does a HydraFacial Treatment take?</h2>\n<p>The HydraFacial treatment is a quick and economical method. The entire process takes as little as 15 minutes.</p>\n<p>Since we have added other beneficial steps for better results, the whole thing takes about 45 minutes in our clinic. This is only so that you get the ultimate satisfaction with the result.</p>\n<h2>How many HydraFacial treatments are required to notice results?</h2>\n<p>You will definitely attain noticeable skin refinement with each session. An individual with normal, radiant skin may just need a single treatment, and results will appear immediately. This will last a week or longer.</p>\n<p>Anyways, a series of six treatments at intervals of 2-4 weeks is recommended to maintain the disappearance of fine lines, <a href=\"https://akarshanskin.com/our-services/best-wrinkle-treatment-kathmandu/\">wrinkles</a>, and blocked pores.</p>\n<p>After this initial series of treatments, your results will last much longer and you will need only fewer maintenance treatments over time.</p>\n<h2>Hydrafacial Treatment Price in Lalitpur, Kathmandu, Nepal</h2>\n<p>Your skin is the first thing that speaks about you, just like the walls and the paintings hung on them tell about a room. And your skin is going to represent you for a long, long time.</p>\n<p>Needless to say, most people spend a lot more on beauty techniques that barely give them the result they want.</p>\n<h2>Types of Facial with price</h2>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Simple HydraFacial</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs. 2,500 (15 Mins)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>HydraFacial without Mask</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.3,000 (30 Mins)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>HydraFacial With Hydrojelly Mask</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.5,000 (1 Hour Plus)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>HydraFacial Any Type Add Chemical Peel</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.1,000 (Extra)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Simple Hydra With Carbon Laser</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.6,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>HydraFacial With Vampire Facial</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.7,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Carbon laser (Picosecond laser)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.5,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Vampire Facial (Prp Micro needling)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rs.6,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2><span>But because technology has come so forwards in today’s age, efficient procedures are also available at a minimal cost.</span></h2>								</div>\n				</div>\n					</div>\n		</div>\n					</div>\n		</section>\n				</div>\n		\n	</div><!-- .entry-content -->\n\n	</article><!-- #post-2753 -->\n\r\n					</div>', 'Hydra Facial in Nepal | Dr. Rajan Tajhya Skin Clinic', '&quot;Revitalize your skin with HydraFacial treatment at Dr Rajan Clinic in Lalitpur. Enjoy glowing, hydrated skin, suitable for all skin types!', 0, 1, 26, '2026-10-03 11:10:31', '2026-10-03 11:10:31'),
